From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: allwinner: A733 combo-PHY -- hand COMB0 back to USB3 when DP alt mode leaves

[Recipe cut: regenerated against the instrumentation-free driver; the hunks that
touched the debug instrumentation are gone.]

After a DisplayPort sink leaves the Type-C port, a SuperSpeed device plugged
into the same port enumerated at 480M on the xHCI high-speed bus. The driver
said so itself on every unplug: "DP alt mode left, COMB0 links back in reset;
SuperSpeed does not return without a phy_exit()/phy_init() cycle".

WHY, READ IN THE CODE AND SEEN AT THE REGISTER
----------------------------------------------

  - The mux callback's return to TYPEC_STATE_SAFE/USB ran
    a733_combophy_dp_teardown() and stopped there. The teardown writes
    LINK_CTRL0 = 0, which holds COMB0_PHY_RESET_N and PIPE_LINK_RESET_N_SOFT
    low. UM V1.00 18.2.6.6 (PDF p. 1176): PHY_RESET_N resets all PHY
    logic except the APB registers and the TAP controller, so the PMA also keeps the DP rate and swing configuration.
  - The only code that releases those resets for USB is
    a733_combophy_reset_seq(), reached only from phy_ops.init.
  - phy_init() calls .init only for the first reference
    (drivers/phy/phy-core.c, the init_count == 0 test). dwc3 takes that
    reference in dwc3_core_init() and holds it while bound; the DP
    transmitter's phy_init()/phy_exit() on the same PHY only move the count
    (sun60i_dp_link_release() says so). An orientation change on the next
    plug runs a733_combophy_param_config() and no reset release either.

So the xHCI SuperSpeed port was left on a PHY held in reset until dwc3 was
rebound.

WHAT SILICON SAID
-----------------

6 GiB board, kernel 6.18.53, 2026-09-27: after the DP
sink left, an RTL9210 Gen 2 enclosure on the same port enumerated at 480M in
both plug orientations. A dwc3 unbind/bind brought it up at 10000M, uas, with
no reboot, LINK_CTRL0 0x00000111, LINK_STUS0 0x00000111.

The failing state was then read on the same board and kernel after a fresh
DP cycle (same day), and it is the mechanism above, observed at
the register: after the unplug LINK_CTRL0 reads 0x00000000 (PHY_RESET_N and
PIPE_LINK_RESET_N_SOFT low) and LINK_STUS0 0x00000000 (PMA_CMN_READY 0).
With the enclosure plugged in the other orientation, PMA index 0xC010 moves
from the DP value 0x51D9 to the USB3 value 0x5100 -- the orientation switch
re-ran the USB3 PMA table -- while LINK_CTRL0 stays 0x00000000 and the device
comes up at 480M. The USB3 table alone does not bring SuperSpeed back.

With this patch, same board and day, kernel 6.18.53-358ssreturn
(Image sha256 d6b771f8...a2a5c): three DP
unplugs, each followed by "DP alt mode left, COMB0 handed back to USB3 by a
PHY exit/init cycle: LINK_CTRL0 0x00001111 / 0x00000111 ... (want the same,
PMA_CMN_READY set)", and then the RTL9210 enclosure at 10000 on the xHCI
SuperSpeed bus, PORTSC2 0x00001603 (U0, speed 5), no rebind. In all three
runs the enclosure went in the SAME orientation as the DP cable (once
reverse, twice normal). DP entered again twice from the USB state
(LINK_CTRL0 0x00000131, PMA 0xC010 back at the DP value 0x51D9). The
opposite orientation was not measured; that path carries the live
TYPEC_CONN_DIR flip, which an earlier investigation covers.

WHAT THIS DOES
--------------

  - On the return to USB, after the teardown and the lane-map restore, the
    mux callback runs this driver's own exit body and then its own init
    body: IDDQ on, the DCXO_SERDES0 gate off and this driver's reference on
    the SERDES config clock dropped (CLK_SERDES_PHY_CFG is shared with COMB1
    and the AUX/HPD PHY, so only the DCXO gate is sure to go off), then
    clocks on, IDDQ clear, PIPE route, the USB3 PMA table and the PIPE
    handshake -- what phy_init() runs, and the PHY half of the rebind that
    was measured to recover. The PMA writes land on a link held in reset, as
    the DP rate table's do.
  - The shape is mainline's qmp_combo_typec_mux_set()
    (drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c): on a change of mode it powers
    the USB half off, runs com_exit()/com_init() and powers it on again from
    inside the mux callback, with dwc3 left running. A reset of the whole
    block, which com_init() does there, is not available here:
    RST_BUS_SERDES is shared with the serdes-ccu.
  - The exit body is factored out of phy_ops.exit as
    a733_combophy_power_down(). .exit now skips it when the USB return's
    bring-up has failed, because that error path has already dropped the
    clocks.
  - The diagnostic line stays and says what happened instead:
    "DP alt mode left, COMB0 handed back to USB3 by a PHY exit/init cycle:
    LINK_CTRL0 ... LINK_STUS0 ... (want ..., PMA_CMN_READY set|NOT set)".
    When no consumer has run phy_init() the old reset-only path remains and
    says so; the DP debug instrumentation's own line points at it.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO
---------------------

  - It does not reset the controller. In the three measured runs (same
    orientation) that was not needed; the reason it could still be is this.
    UM V1.00 18.2.6.6 (PDF p. 1176), bit 0 COMB0_PHY_RESET_N: when the
    reset is released, all PHY inputs must be at the levels the PIPE
    specification gives for a PIPE reset. The rebind meets that: it asserts and
    releases the controller reset (dwc3-generic-plat.c:54-61), runs
    dwc3_core_init() with its CSFTRST before a role is set (core.c:2367
    before :2376; dwc3_core_soft_reset() returns early once the role is
    host, :331-332), then the xHCI's HCRST, and only after all of that does
    the PHY come out of reset. This patch releases PHY_RESET_N while dwc3
    keeps running and drives the PIPE inputs from whatever state its link is
    in. Bit 5 on the same page adds the second half: with
    PIPE_LINK_RESET_N_USB3P1_MASK = 0 and PIPE_LINK_RESET_N_SOFT = 1, which
    is how a733_combophy_reset_seq() leaves them, the PIPE link reset is
    the one USB3P1 outputs to PHY0 -- a line the controller
    drives and this driver cannot pulse. Which dwc3 event toggles it is not
    in the UM (18.4.4.2 defers the controller to the Synopsys databook).
    Hence the falsifier below: PMA_CMN_READY set and the device still at
    480M means the controller half is missing.
  - It does not put back the seven PMA words the DP writes reach and the USB3
    table does not: 0x004B, 0x4011, 0xE003 (PHY_PMA_PLL_RAW_CTRL in the
    Torrent map) and TX_DIAG_ACYA on the four lanes. The rebind does not
    write them either, and SuperSpeed ran at 10000 after it (same day,
    orientation normal). 0xE003 read 0x0003 there, and it reads 0x0003 after
    a cold boot with no DP entry as well (2026-09-27), so
    that one is the USB value too, not a DP leftover.
  - After a failed return (the bring-up error path), a dwc3 rebind is not
    enough while the DP transmitter still holds its reference: phy_init()
    reaches .init only from init_count 0. SuperSpeed then returns once every
    consumer has released the PHY, and the error line says so.
  - A SAFE notify with the sink still attached now also reloads the USB3
    table: dp_altmode_configure_vdm() sends one before every Configure
    (drivers/usb/typec/altmodes/displayport.c:238). DisplayPort gets its rate
    table back through phy_configure() on the next training, the same split
    qmp_combo_typec_mux_set() has between the mux re-init and the DP
    controller's configure.
  - It keeps no IDDQ dwell time. The rebind held the PHY down for about 2 s;
    nothing in the UM asks for a minimum, and none is invented here.
  - It uses the orientation the DP cable had. A device plugged the other way
    round goes through a733_combophy_typec_set(), the same path as a reversed
    device plugged after a cold boot: a live read-modify-write of
    TYPEC_CONN_DIR, which UM 18.2.6.6 bit 12 does not allow.

THE VENDOR
----------

Read as a hint (bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c, the vendor BSP
kernel): it has no return path. Its DP set_mode for pin assignments C and E
touches only TYPEC_CONN_DIR (sunxi_cadence_combo0_dp_phy_set_mode()), and its
USB set_mode re-runs combo0_usb_param_config() on a change of orientation or
state but never the reset handshake
(sunxi_cadence_combo0_usb_phy_set_mode()). Nothing here is taken from it.

THE PROOF
---------

Test kernel with this patch, localversion -358ssreturn, no rebind.
Instrument: a script. Steps 0-2 are done (6 GiB board,
2026-09-27, see WHAT SILICON SAID); step 3 is open: it also goes through the
live TYPEC_CONN_DIR flip, which is handled separately.

  0. After the cold boot, before the first DP entry: a snapshot of the
     registers above as the USB-only baseline (0xE003 included).
  1. DP sink on the Type-C port, link trained. Unplug it. The kernel log
     carries the new line with PMA_CMN_READY set and LINK_CTRL0 equal to its
     want value.
  2. A SuperSpeed device into the same port in the SAME orientation as the
     DP cable: 5000 or 10000 on the xHCI SuperSpeed bus, PORTSC2 PLS 0. No
     orientation change, so this is the path this patch adds and nothing
     else.
  3. The same with the device in the OPPOSITE orientation to the DP cable.
     This one also goes through the live TYPEC_CONN_DIR flip.

Falsifiers: the device at 480M on the HS bus with PMA_CMN_READY set (the
controller needs a reset too), or PMA_CMN_READY NOT set in the new line (the
PHY cycle is not enough). If it is the first, unbind and bind xhci-hcd.1.auto
alone before anything else: that is an HCRST with no CSFTRST and no PHY
cycle (xhci-plat takes its root-hub PHY reference with dwc3's still held, so
phy_init() never reaches .init), and it separates the xHCI port state from
dwc3's PIPE reset. Only then a dwc3 rebind.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff -u a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
@@ -1685,16 +1685,30 @@ static int a733_combophy_init(struct phy *phy)
 	return ret;
 }
 
-static int a733_combophy_exit(struct phy *phy)
+/* phy_ops.exit's body, and the first half of the cycle the mux runs when DP
+ * alt mode hands the lanes back. Caller holds cp->lock.
+ */
+static void a733_combophy_power_down(struct a733_combophy *cp)
 {
-	struct a733_combophy *cp = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
-
-	mutex_lock(&cp->lock);
-	cp->inited = false;
 	a733_rmw(cp->link, COMB0_LINK_CTRL2, 0,
 		 PHY0_IDDQ_EN_SEL | PHY0_IDDQ_EN_SOFT);	/* IDDQ = power down */
 	clk_disable_unprepare(cp->dcxo_clk);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(cp->serdes_clk);
+}
+
+static int a733_combophy_exit(struct phy *phy)
+{
+	struct a733_combophy *cp = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+
+	mutex_lock(&cp->lock);
+	/* inited is false here only if the mux's USB return failed its
+	 * bring-up, which has already dropped the clocks; dropping them again
+	 * would unbalance them.
+	 */
+	if (cp->inited) {
+		cp->inited = false;
+		a733_combophy_power_down(cp);
+	}
 	mutex_unlock(&cp->lock);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -1822,6 +1836,90 @@ static void a733_combophy_dp_lanes_leave(struct a733_combophy *cp)
 	cp->dp_lanes_saved = false;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Hand COMB0 back to the USB3 consumer when DP alt mode leaves.
+ *
+ * WHY THE TEARDOWN ALONE LEAVES SUPERSPEED DOWN. a733_combophy_dp_teardown()
+ * writes LINK_CTRL0 = 0, which holds COMB0_PHY_RESET_N and
+ * PIPE_LINK_RESET_N_SOFT low. PHY_RESET_N resets all PHY logic except the
+ * APB registers and the TAP controller (UM
+ * V1.00 18.2.6.6, PDF p. 1176), so the PMA keeps the DP configuration. The
+ * only code that releases
+ * those resets for USB is a733_combophy_reset_seq(), reached only from
+ * phy_ops.init, and phy_init() calls .init only for the first reference
+ * (drivers/phy/phy-core.c, init_count == 0). dwc3 holds that reference as long
+ * as it is bound, and the DP transmitter's own phy_init()/phy_exit() only move
+ * the count. So nothing re-ran the USB bring-up, and the xHCI SuperSpeed port
+ * was left on a PHY held in reset.
+ *
+ * WHAT THIS DOES. The PHY half of the cycle a dwc3 unbind/bind was measured to
+ * recover from:
+ * this driver's exit body, then its init body -- IDDQ on, the DCXO_SERDES0
+ * gate off and this driver's reference on the SERDES config clock dropped
+ * (COMB1 and the AUX/HPD PHY hold that clock too, so it keeps running), then
+ * clocks, IDDQ clear, PIPE route, the USB3 PMA table and the PIPE handshake,
+ * i.e. exactly what phy_init() runs. The shape is mainline's
+ * qmp_combo_typec_mux_set() (drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c), which
+ * on a change of mode powers the USB half off, runs com_exit()/com_init() and
+ * powers it on again from inside the mux callback, with dwc3 left running. It
+ * cannot be qmp's reset of the whole block: RST_BUS_SERDES is shared with the
+ * serdes-ccu, see the file header.
+ *
+ * What it does not do:
+ *  - reset the controller side. For bit 0 the same UM entry requires the
+ *    PHY inputs to sit at the PIPE specification's PIPE-reset levels when
+ *    the reset is released. A rebind meets that, it re-runs dwc3
+ *    from scratch; here dwc3 keeps running and drives the PIPE inputs from
+ *    whatever state it is in. And with bit 5 MASK = 0 and bit 4 SOFT = 1, as
+ *    a733_combophy_reset_seq() leaves them, the PIPE link reset comes from
+ *    the USB3 controller (bit 5, same page), which this driver cannot pulse.
+ *  - put back the seven PMA words the DP rate and swing writes reach and the
+ *    USB3 table does not (0x004B, 0x4011, 0xE003, and TX_DIAG_ACYA on the
+ *    four lanes). A dwc3 rebind does not write them either, and SuperSpeed
+ *    ran at 10000 after it (2026-09-27). 0xE003 read 0x0003 there, which is
+ *    also its value after a cold boot with no DP entry (same day),
+ *    so not a DP leftover.
+ *
+ * Caller holds cp->lock and has run the teardown, so the PMA writes below land
+ * on a link held in reset, as the DP rate table's do.
+ */
+static void a733_combophy_usb_return(struct a733_combophy *cp)
+{
+	u32 want, stus;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!cp->inited) {
+		dev_info(cp->dev,
+			 "DP alt mode left, COMB0 links back in reset; no consumer has run phy_init(), SuperSpeed returns with the next one\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	a733_combophy_power_down(cp);
+	ret = a733_combophy_bringup(cp);
+	if (ret) {
+		cp->inited = false;
+		dev_err(cp->dev,
+			"DP alt mode left, USB3 bring-up failed (%d): COMB0 stays powered down, SuperSpeed returns only once every consumer has released the PHY and phy_init() runs again\n",
+			ret);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/* The USB end state of LINK_CTRL0: 0x00001111 with a reversed plug and
+	 * SuperSpeed at 10000 (measured 2026-08-19),
+	 * 0x00000111 with a normal one after the dwc3 rebind (measured
+	 * 2026-09-27).
+	 */
+	want = PHY0_RESET_N | PHY0_PIPE_LINK_RESET_N_SOFT |
+	       PHY0_DP_LINK_RESET_N_SOFT |
+	       (cp->orientation == TYPEC_ORIENTATION_REVERSE ?
+		PHY0_TYPEC_CONN_DIR : 0);
+	stus = readl(cp->link + COMB0_LINK_STUS0);
+	dev_info(cp->dev,
+		 "DP alt mode left, COMB0 handed back to USB3 by a PHY exit/init cycle: LINK_CTRL0 0x%08x LINK_STUS0 0x%08x (want 0x%08x, PMA_CMN_READY %s)\n",
+		 readl(cp->link + COMB0_LINK_CTRL0), stus, want,
+		 stus & PHY0_PMA_CMN_READY ? "set" : "NOT set");
+}
+
 /* COMB0 carries either SuperSpeed or DP, never both, and the lane routing lives
  * inside this PHY -- there is no external mux on this board. So the DisplayPort
  * alt-mode driver reaches the lanes through here, and this callback is the only
@@ -1847,6 +1945,10 @@ static void a733_combophy_dp_lanes_leave(struct a733_combophy *cp)
  * front end at 0x06C01E00 (0x03331131 in the capture, 0x00330000 at reset),
  * which belongs to the separate AUX/HPD PHY, and the swing/pre-emphasis tables.
  *
+ * Leaving DP -- TYPEC_STATE_SAFE, which tcpm_reset_port() sends on detach, or
+ * TYPEC_STATE_USB -- tears the link down and hands COMB0 back to USB3 through
+ * a733_combophy_usb_return().
+ *
  * Returning 0 rather than an error stays deliberate: an error aborts the
  * alt-mode entry, and then nothing is learned about what the sink offers.
  */
@@ -1869,8 +1971,7 @@ static int a733_combophy_typec_mux_set(struct typec_mux_dev *mux,
 			a733_combophy_dp_lanes_leave(cp);
 			cp->dp_active = false;
 			cp->dp_handshake_ok = false;
-			dev_info(cp->dev,
-				 "DP alt mode left, COMB0 links back in reset; SuperSpeed does not return without a phy_exit()/phy_init() cycle\n");
+			a733_combophy_usb_return(cp);
 		}
 		goto out;
 	}
